            <ArticleTitle>Elevated levels of C-reactive protein before coronary artery bypass grafting predict recurrence of ischemic events.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>459-61, A9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>C-reactive protein was measured in 86 patients undergoing coronary artery bypass graft surgery. Patients were followed up for 3.2 years (range 1 to 6). Patients with C-reactive protein &gt; or = 3 mg/L had significantly increased risk of recurrent ischemia at 1 to 6 years after intervention.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
